From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 10:20:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] gpl: -clusters_file, groups of cells pulled toward an anchor
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Nesterov placement minimises the sum of wirelength plus a density
penalty. A module whose partners sit on opposite sides of the die is
spread between them by that sum, and the paths inside it pay: on
XiangShan's XSTile parent, CtrlBlock's cells fill 8 % of their bounding
box and its worst paths are a wall of control logic at 2,406 ps, where
the same module placed alone closes at 1,200 ps.

global_placement -clusters_file <json> names groups of cells by
instance-name prefix; each group's cells are pulled toward its anchor,
or its own centroid when it has none:

  {"tau_iter": 0,
   "clusters": [{"name": "CtrlBlock",
                 "prefixes": ["core/backend/inner_ctrlBlock"],
                 "anchor_um": [1200, 1250],
                 "weight": 1.0}]}

A prefix matches the instance of that name and every instance under
it (prefix/...); the longest matching prefix wins. The pull is the
descent direction of k * |x - a|^2, k chosen so that a cell one RMS
radius from the centroid is pulled with `weight` times the mean
wirelength gradient. It is added to the sum gradient before the
preconditioner, so the step length, the backtracking and the snapshots
see it as they see the wirelength and density terms. With tau_iter > 0
it decays as exp(-iter / tau_iter): a short tau shapes the start of
placement and lets go, as DG-RePlAce's cluster constraint does (Kahng
et al., IEEE TCAD 2024); 0 holds the group to the end. The file is
meant to come from the macro placer's clustering (rtl_macro_placer),
which already places standard-cell clusters as soft macros.

The file is read once. Which group each gcell is in is matched again,
by instance name, after any change to the gcell list (a timing-driven
repair's buffers, routability's fillers): every such change goes
through the parallel-vector bookkeeping, which marks the groups stale.

Hard stops: an unreadable file (GPL-0343), a malformed one (GPL-0344:
not JSON, no clusters array, a key missing or of the wrong type, a
negative weight, an anchor that is not [x, y]), a group that matches no
cell (GPL-0342). CPU only: the GPU path refuses it (GPL-0340). Without
-clusters_file nothing changes: gpl's test logs are those of the change
before this one.

On XSTile's parent, six groups (dispatch, decode, rename, memCtrl, the
13 integer issue queues, fusionDecoder; weight 1, no fade), measured
with this change written against an earlier OpenROAD: the reg2reg
excess over 2,000 ps fell 36 %; adding the ROB (658,000 cells) diverged
(GPL-0307).

cohesion_test: a group of gcd's cells ends up tighter (RMS radius
-14 % at weight 1, -73 % at weight 4), an anchor draws its centroid,
a short tau lets go, the groups follow the cells when the gcell list
changes under them, and every bad file stops.

Not upstreamed. Carried in bazel-orfs to measure on XiangShan, applied
after the other carried OpenROAD patches (last, after 0240); retires at
a //:bump onto an OpenROAD that has it, or is dropped if the
measurements do not hold.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
